 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "ConnectFourBoard(rows, cols) creates a rows x cols board of \"0\" cells; row 0 is the top row. drop(color, col) places a one-letter color in the lowest empty cell of column col (unchanged when the column is full) and returns a fresh copy of the whole board as rows of one-character strings. getWinner() returns the color of the first piece that completed four or more equal colors in a row horizontally, vertically or diagonally, or \"0\" when no line exists yet; the winner never changes afterwards and drops continue to work. Every method call is answered in call order on one instance; void methods return nothing.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk15-a-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
